---
/**
 * The home page hero (only the home page sets `hero` in its frontmatter).
 *
 * Left: what Axcess is and the two next steps. Right: a picture of a report,
 * drawn in HTML rather than a screenshot so it stays sharp, follows the
 * light and dark theme, and can be kept in step with the app's wording.
 * Sizes, spacing, layering and shadows started from the v3 design artifact;
 * the home page section in theme.css lists what differs and why.
 *
 * Choices and why:
 * - One filled button ("Download Axcess"). It goes to the download section
 *   rather than straight to a file: guessing the system can't tell an Intel
 *   Mac from Apple silicon, and only Apple silicon is built, so a direct
 *   file link would hand some readers a file that won't open.
 * - The second button goes to "What Axcess checks", the honest coverage
 *   numbers, because the next question after "what is it" is "what does it
 *   miss" (Articulating Design Decisions: answer the objection early).
 * - The mockup uses a made-up site (www.example.org, reserved by RFC 2606)
 *   and only words the app really shows (the Issues and Inspector screens).
 *   The back panel is the top of a report's Issues page, drawn as close to
 *   the app as the panel's size allows (developer's direction, 2026-10-19):
 *   the trail ("Reports", the site, "Report #12"), the "Issues" title, the
 *   date line, the Export report button, and the three numbers as the app
 *   shows them (ReportSummary.tsx): no tiles, the number in navy, its name,
 *   and one line under it. It used to show three tinted tiles (Pages, Page
 *   states opened by clicking, Mostly sure issues), the app's old summary.
 *   At a narrow width the numbers go two and one, as in the app.
 *   It is one image to assistive technology, with a text description, so a
 *   screen reader does not read out a fake interface piece by piece
 *   (role="img" with aria-label, WCAG technique ARIA6; SC 1.1.1 Non-text
 *   Content, Level A).
 * - "WCAG" links to its glossary entry, which spells it out (SC 3.1.4
 *   Abbreviations, Level AAA, technique G55). The badge says only "Free and
 *   open source" so it stays one line at 320 px.
 *
 * Calmer, by the developer's direction (2026-10-06):
 * - The heading is semibold (650), not bold, and a little smaller, and the
 *   paragraph is held to about 60 characters a line. At full weight the
 *   heading, the name in the header and the button all competed.
 * - No arrow on "Download Axcess": the words already say it, and the "↓"
 *   character drew clumsily in this font.
 * - The four facts are a 2 by 2 grid, each with a check mark, instead of a
 *   wrapping line that left one fact alone on the second row. All four stay,
 *   including the WCAG version, because it is a limit (docs/plain-language.md
 *   rule 12). At 320 px they become one column.
 * - The two report panels have one width, and the front one is offset 40
 *   px to the right and down. The old front panel stuck out 28 px to the
 *   left, toward the text, and was wider, so it read as a mistake. Tried
 *   and rejected: an inset front panel (the back card's corner showed) and
 *   a flush one (it read as one tall card with a seam). The offset is big
 *   enough to look meant and points away from the text. Below 30rem the
 *   panels go flush, so nothing needs sideways scrolling (SC 1.4.10
 *   Reflow, Level AA).
 */
import { url } from "../lib/site";

const { hero, title } = Astro.locals.starlightRoute.entry.data;
---

<section class="hero not-content" aria-labelledby="_top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="copy">
      <p class="badge">Free and open source</p>
      <h1 id="_top">{hero?.title ?? title}</h1>
      {hero?.tagline && <p class="tagline">{hero.tagline}</p>}
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={url("/get-started/#download")}>Download Axcess</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={url("/coverage/")}>See what it checks</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="facts">
        <li><span>Runs on your own computer</span></li>
        <li><span>No account needed</span></li>
        <li><span>Mac, Windows and Linux</span></li>
        <li><span>Checks <a href={url("/docs/glossary/#wcag")}>WCAG</a> 2.1 AA, or 2.2 if you choose</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div
      class="mockup"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Example of the Issues page of an Axcess report for www.example.org: 12 kinds of issue found, in 386 places, on 194 pages visited plus 1,171 page states opened by clicking. In front of it, the saved copy of a page outlines the first of 19 flagged elements, a link, and lists what it is, its text, its size and its element locator."
    >
      <div class="panel summary" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="trail">
          <span class="crumb-link">Reports</span>
          <svg class="crumb-sep" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg>
          <span class="crumb-site">www.example.org</span>
          <span class="crumb-tag">Report #12</span>
        </div>
        <div class="report">
          <div class="report-head">
            <div>
              <p class="report-title">Issues</p>
              <p class="report-date">Based on the report generated Oct 6, 2026, 04:24 PM</p>
            </div>
            <span class="export"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/><path d="m7 10 5 5 5-5"/><path d="M12 15V3"/></svg>Export report<svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <div class="stats">
            <div><span class="n">12</span><span class="l">Kinds of issue found</span><span class="d">One per row in the table below</span></div>
            <div><span class="n">386</span><span class="l">Places issues appear (occurrences)</span><span class="d">Each one is an element on a page</span></div>
            <div class="pages"><span class="n">194</span><span class="l">Pages visited</span><span class="d">Plus 1,171 page states opened by clicking</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel inspector" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="bar">
          <span>Flagged element 1 of 19</span>
          <span class="chips"><span class="chip muted"><svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m18 15-6-6-6 6"/></svg>Previous</span><span class="chip">Next<svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></span></span>
        </div>
        <dl class="facts-list">
          <dt>What it is</dt><dd>Link</dd>
          <dt>Text or label</dt><dd>“Copy link to this heading”</dd>
          <dt>Size</dt><dd>30 pixels wide, 30 pixels tall</dd>
          <dt>Element locator (CSS selector)</dt><dd class="mono">…our-post &gt; .copy-link-btn.before.auto-heading-links--iconcolor</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="saved-copy">
          <p class="page-heading">Using editors to build accessible pages</p>
          <span class="tag">1 of 19</span>
          <div class="row">
            <span class="target"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M19 21l-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/></svg></span>
            <span class="page-sub">Give your post a clear title</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hero {
    background: var(--h-page);
  }
  .wrap {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 80px 32px 88px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 460px), 1fr));
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 6px 14px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--h-tint);
    color: var(--h-accent);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 22px 0 20px;
    color: var(--h-text);
    font-size: clamp(38px, 4.6vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: 1.06;
    letter-spacing: -0.024em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .tagline {
    max-width: 32rem;
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    color: var(--h-muted);
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  /* The artifact's two buttons. Links, because both go somewhere. */
  .button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    min-height: var(--ax-target);
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .button:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
  .primary {
    padding: 16px 26px;
    background: var(--h-primary-bg);
    color: var(--h-primary-fg);
  }
  .primary:hover {
    background: var(--h-primary-hover);
  }
  .secondary {
    padding: 15px 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--h-button-line);
    background: var(--h-band);
    color: var(--h-accent);
  }
  .secondary:hover {
    border-color: var(--h-accent);
  }
  .facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, max-content);
    gap: 10px 28px;
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    color: var(--h-muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .facts li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  /* A check mark drawn in CSS, so it is decoration a screen reader skips. */
  .facts li::before {
    content: "";
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 10px;
    height: 5px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--h-accent);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--h-accent);
    transform: translateY(-3px) rotate(-45deg);
  }
  .facts a {
    color: var(--h-accent);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  /* Mockup */
  .mockup {
    position: relative;
  }
  .panel {
    border: 1px solid var(--h-card-line);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--h-band);
  }
  /* Two panels of one width, offset 40 px right and down, so the front
     one reads as a closer look laid on the report. */
  .summary {
    container-type: inline-size;
    margin-inline-end: 40px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--h-shadow-soft);
  }
  /* The app's top bar: the trail, on the bar's white, over a line. */
  .trail {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 12px 22px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--h-divider);
    color: var(--h-text);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .crumb-link {
    color: var(--h-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
  }
  .crumb-sep {
    width: 13px;
    height: 13px;
    color: var(--h-muted);
  }
  .crumb-tag {
    padding: 2px 7px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--h-tint);
  }
  /* The page under it, on the app's page grey. */
  /* The 52px at the foot sits behind the front panel. */
  .report {
    padding: 18px 22px 52px;
    background: var(--h-page);
  }
  .report-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .report-title {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--h-text);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .report-date {
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    color: var(--h-muted);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .export {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 7px 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--h-chip-line);
    border-radius: 7px;
    background: var(--h-band);
    color: var(--h-text);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .export svg {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
  }
  /* The app's three numbers (ReportSummary.tsx): no panel, the number
     first and largest in navy, its name, then one line in the muted
     colour; the space between the columns does the grouping. */
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 18px 20px;
    padding: 22px 0 6px;
  }
  .stats > div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3px;
  }
  .n {
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    color: var(--h-accent);
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: 1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .l {
    color: var(--h-text);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .d {
    color: var(--h-muted);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  /* Narrow, as in the app below 640px: the two issue numbers share a row,
     and the pages take the row under them. */
  @container (max-width: 27rem) {
    .stats {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
    .stats .pages {
      grid-column: span 2;
    }
    .report-head {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
  .inspector {
    position: relative;
    margin: -32px 0 0 40px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--h-shadow);
  }
  .bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--h-divider);
    color: var(--h-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .chips {
    display: flex;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .chip {
    padding: 5px 11px;
    border: 1px solid var(--h-chip-line);
    border-radius: 7px;
    color: var(--h-text);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  /* The artifact greys out "Previous" because it is the first element. It
     is part of a picture (role="img"), so its contrast is decoration, but
     it still uses the muted text colour (8:1 or more), not a paler grey. */
  .chip.muted {
    color: var(--h-muted);
  }
  .facts-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 6px 24px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--h-divider);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  dt {
    color: var(--h-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--h-text);
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .mono {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
  }
  /* The saved copy of a page, with the app's maize outline and navy tag. */
  .saved-copy {
    padding: 22px 24px 28px;
    background: var(--h-saved);
  }
  .page-heading {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    color: var(--h-saved-link);
    font-size: clamp(18px, 1.9vw, 22px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border: 3px solid #f5c400;
    border-radius: 6px 6px 0 0;
    background: #0a2647;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  /* The flagged element, drawn as the app's Page inspector shows it: a maize
     ring and a navy inner line around the element itself, here the page's
     "Copy link to this heading" button, a 30 by 30 pixel square showing a
     bookmark icon (the page's own icon, so drawn in a page blue, not the
     app's navy). An empty box, and then a wide box with a link icon, were
     tried; both differed from the real screen (developer's review with
     screenshots, 2026-10-06). Decoration inside a picture that already has
     a text description. */
  .target {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    color: #1d5fbf;
    border: 4px solid #f5c400;
    border-radius: 2px;
    outline: 3px solid #0a2647;
    outline-offset: -7px;
    background: #ffffff;
  }
  .target svg {
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
  }
  /* The inspector's Previous and Next carry chevrons, as in the app:
     Previous points up, and Next opens a list of the flagged elements. */
  .chip {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .chev {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
  }
  .page-sub {
    color: var(--h-saved-link);
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.7vw, 20px);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .wrap {
      padding: 56px 20px 64px;
    }
    .facts {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .summary {
      margin-inline-end: 0;
    }
    .inspector {
      margin-inline-start: 0;
    }
    /* Stacked buttons at one width, not two ragged widths. */
    .actions {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .button {
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .facts-list {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 2px;
    }
    dd + dt {
      margin-top: 8px;
    }
  }
</style>
